My current Valk is at 30XL and +20 Wisdom, with no metal armor,
and even the simplest spells are still at 30% failure rate.
with exercise, I could improve attack and escape spells
(currently at unskilled), but I doubt even then that I could get
good enough at any higher level skills to be able to use them
during a fight, when you can't afford retries.

IMHO, a Valk can only really be a spellcaster (and not a really
good one at that) with a robe.  Which in turn means GDSM for
armor, for magic resistance.  (That's my usual prefered
combination, but since I've not seen a single gray dragon in
this game, nor any other means of reflection, I took advantage
of the silver dragon's scales, and wished up a cloak of magic
resistence when I got to the castle.)

In the end: a Valk can easily get something between 250-300
hitpoints, just by leveling up and drinking the various healing
potions which come her way.  Getting an AC of -25, -30 isn't too
hard either, even without a shield.  The quest artifact gives
half damage.  And a Valk can get expert with some really good
artifact weapons, and skilled at two weaponing.  Which pretty
much means that she doesn't have to worry too much about
anything which just classically attacks, and that's a fair
percentage of what's out there.  Add to it that she can become
expert at throwing daggers, for those monsters which have
special attacks which means that you don't want to get too
close, and it becomes clear that spell casting doesn't play a
major role.  (I like the combination with the robe because it
allows me to get cure sickness to 0%.  And while it's not a
spell that I use very often, the couple of times I've used it,
it has saved my life.  And I don't think I'm going to get it
there in this game, so I'm starting to think about what my
alternatives might be.)

